</figure>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS11" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.11 </span>Regression <em id="A1.SS11.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">vs</em>.<span id="A1.SS11.3" class="ltx_text"></span> classification-type confidence loss</h3>

<div id="A1.SS11.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS11.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Here we ablate the type of confidence loss used during training. Table <a href="#A1.T9" title="Table 9 ‣ A.11 Regression vs. classification-type confidence loss ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Generative Point Tracking with Flow Matching" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> shows our quantitative results in a shortened training setup, as described previously. On average, the regression-based approach results in higher point tracking accuracy than the classification-based approach.</p>
</div>
